{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/actions/setup-bazel/action.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:26:26.947334Z","id":"38a0bfb47af606342a5e4c81693fb2847e6442e5dc80f78a2895bac2e1ab584e","body":{"detail":"../changelist bounds its disk at 12 GB; this repository's state adds Chromium (@chromium//:browsers), two npm trees and the release build (//crates/clax-cli:clax_opt). The step writes the disk's size to the job summary on every run: set the bound from what main's runs show, and from Blacksmith's per-disk size limit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"f2b385da2d73d530b2c4ffeb7f04b34dd2c3f173e1b1c360938c770a4ea4b128"},"summary":"The sticky disk's 20 GB bound is a guess: no run has measured what Bazel's output base, downloads and Chromium take on a runner","tags":["ci","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/actions/setup-bazel/action.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T03:41:50.177283Z","id":"a1ee2d53cb16cd178351eb449b00c6ce39675a53db2b3a2ab6b01a685a423007","body":{"detail":"useblacksmith/stickydisk (src/post.ts at 3f6be1451e3cad893b778bc93495c80452a5da26) decides on the runner whether to commit, from the commit input, and the host refuses only under its own policy, such as branch protection. clax is public and on: pull_request runs a pull request's own copy of this action and of .github/workflows/ci.yml, so a pull request that is allowed to run can set commit to true, or call the commit RPC from a test, and write main's disk (key <repo>-bazel-bazel-<hash of .bazelversion>). The next push to main then builds from it. perf-log no longer holds a write token (perf-log-publish appends the record from a fresh checkout), so the exposure is tampered build results, not the repository. To close: turn on Blacksmith's sticky-disk branch protection for main, keep fork pull request workflows requiring approval, and check that a pull request's run logs that its sticky-disk changes will not be committed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"6682228a1484b54f74719d47682f5f8e59b557f7279aa7851832dda08bf4d968"},"summary":"Pull requests' writes to the sticky disk are stopped only on the client unless Blacksmith's sticky-disk branch protection is on","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
